   142 				; Constant-source fill for the menu separator row - unused at boot now (the
   143 				; separator is assembly-embedded, see Load_Menu_Sep in init_vbxe.asm), so
   144 				; Fill_Pal_Preview_Cmap (view1024.asm) repurposes it for the P-preview's
   145 				; CRAM_Buffer attribute fills (patching Dest_Adr, Dest_Step_Y0/1, Blt_W0/1,
   146 				; Blt_H, Blt_Xor).  BCB budget: everything in this file must fit $100-$1FF
   147 				; of VBXE VRAM (see the memory-map comment at the top of view1024.asm) - an
   148 				; overflow past $200 runs into the NTSC_Palette load and corrupts it (this
   149 				; happened once).  Removing the old banner blank-fill BCB freed one 21-byte
   150 				; slot; check the .lab before adding another.
