   916 				; Sets 1-3 are pure single-component ramps - set 1 colour i = (i,0,0), set 2 =
   917 				; (0,i,0), set 3 = (0,0,i) - so they are generated straight into the registers
   918 				; rather than stored.  Y walks CR/CG/CB (consecutive registers) for each colour;
   919 				; the component whose register matches the set gets i, the other two get 0.
   920 				; Plain sta (VBXEBase),y (what vbsta expands to) so Y can be the register index.
   921 3655 A9 01			lda #$01
   922 3657 85 80			sta Reg1							; Reg1 = palette set 1-3
